    "message": {
     "content": "### The Verdict: Outstanding Offer (Top 10% of L6 Band)\n\nThis is an **exceptionally strong offer**. For context, median total compensation for a Google L6 Product Manager in the San Francisco Bay Area is around **$520,000\u2013$580,000/year**. \n\nYour offer averages **~$697,000/year** over 4 years (including the sign-on), with a **Year 1 total compensation exceeding $1,000,000**.\n\n---\n\n### Compensation Breakdown & Comparison\n\nGoogle primarily uses a **front-loaded equity vesting schedule** (most commonly **38% / 32% / 20% / 10%**, or occasionally **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**).\n\nAssuming the standard 38/32/20/10 schedule:\n\n| Component | Your Meta Run-Rate | Google Year 1 | Google Year 2 | Google Year 3 | Google Year 4 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 | $260,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $52,000 (20%) | $52,000 (20%) | $52,000 (20%) | $52,000 (20%) |\n| **RSU Vesting** | ~$250,000 | $509,200 *(38%)* | $428,800 *(32%)* | $268,000 *(20%)* | $134,000 *(10%)* |\n| **Sign-On Bonus**| \u2014 | $200,000 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| **Estimated Refresher Vest** | Included above | \u2014 | ~$15,000\u2013$25,000 | ~$40,000\u2013$60,000 | ~$70,000\u2013$100,000 |\n| **Total Target Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$1,021,200** | **~$755,000+** | **~$620,000+** | **~$516,000+** |\n\n*(Note: Even under Google\u2019s older 33/33/22/12 schedule, your Year 1 equity vest is $442,200, putting Year 1 TC at ~$954,000.)*\n\n---\n\n### Component-by-Component Assessment\n\n1. **Base Salary ($260,000):**\n   * *Assessment:* **Near band cap.** The job band tops out at $271,000; you are at the 88th percentile of the range.\n2. **Sign-On Bonus ($200,000):**\n   * *Assessment:* **Very high.** Typical L6 PM sign-on bonuses range between $50,000 and $120,000. Google is offering $200,000 to offset unvested Meta equity and close you quickly.\n3. **Equity ($1,340,000 / 4 yrs):**\n   * *Assessment:* **High.** Standard initial grants for L6 PMs sit between $800,000 and $1,100,000. At $1.34M, Google is pricing you near the top tier for entry L6.\n\n---\n\n### Should You Accept, Negotiate, or Walk Away?\n\n* **Do not walk away** purely for compensation reasons; this package represents a massive financial acceleration over your current Meta baseline.\n* **You should negotiate.** Since you are happy at Meta, weren\u2019t looking, and hold strong leverage as a high-performing IC6, you have zero downside to asking for more. Google does not rescind offers over polite, market-based counters.\n\n---\n\n### What to Ask For & How to Negotiate\n\nBecause your base ($260k) is almost at the top of the salary posting range ($271k), **focus your negotiation on Equity (RSUs).**\n\n#### The Strategy\n1. **Target Equity:** Ask for **$1,500,000 \u2013 $1,550,000** in GSUs (an increase of ~$160k\u2013$210k over 4 years).\n2. **Leverage Points:**\n   * You were passive and are happy with your current trajectory and team at Meta.\n   * Highlight the backend drop-off in Years 3 and 4 caused by Google's front-loaded vesting schedule.\n   * Frame it as removing any hesitation to leave Meta immediately.\n\n#### Sample Negotiation Script / Email\n\n> *\"Hi [Recruiter Name],*\n>\n> *Thank you for putting this offer together. I\u2019m really excited about the team and the scope of the L6 role in SF.*\n>\n> *As mentioned throughout the process, I\u2019m in a strong position at Meta with solid growth prospects and meaningful unvested equity. Because I wasn\u2019t actively looking, I want to make sure the transition makes complete sense over the full 4-year horizon\u2014especially considering the front-loaded structure where initial grant vesting steps down in Years 3 and 4.*\n>\n> *If we can bring the equity grant to **$1,500,000**, I would be thrilled to sign immediately.*\n>\n> *Let me know if there is flexibility here to close the gap.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Important Things to Clarify Before Signing\n\n1. **Exact Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Ask the recruiter to confirm whether this grant uses the **38/32/20/10** or **33/33/22/12** schedule, and confirm monthly vesting cadence (L6 equity typically vests monthly after the first month/quarter).\n2. **Sign-On Terms & Clawback:**\n   * Verify whether the $200,000 is paid as a lump sum in your first 30 days and confirm the clawback period (standard is 12 months pro-rata).\n3. **Scope and Leveling:**\n   * Meta IC6 is Staff/Principal scope. At Google, L5 is Senior PM and L6 is Staff PM / Group PM. Ensure your title in the offer letter accurately reflects **Staff PM (L6)** rather than Senior PM (L5/L6 misalignment), as internal scope and promotion gates to L7 (Director/Senior Staff) will depend on it.",
